Dear Mara,

My apologies for the long silence. January ran away from me: we lost a reference librarian to retirement and I have been covering the desk two afternoons a week, which is good for the soul and terrible for the inbox.

I have not lost interest in the library research assistant, quite the opposite. But I cannot give it the attention it deserves this side of the break. Let's park this until after midterms - mid-March at the earliest. Still keen. When we do pick it up, I suspect my subject librarians will have opinions about how students actually search, which is rather the point.

And please, whenever you get to the concept note, no rush. I would much rather read something considered than something hurried.

With warm regards,
Ramona

